## std.consortium — shared ownership by reference count.
##
## `Rc of T` keeps a value on the heap with a counter. Copying the handle is
## free (one increment); the value is destroyed when the last owner goes away,
## and the block is released when the last `Weak` stops looking.
##
## ## When to use it
## Use `Rc` when **several** parts of a program must observe the same value and
## you cannot tell which one dies last: a document shared by two views, a node
## referenced by a parent and by a cache, an asset handed to several scenes.
## Use `Arc` when the owners live on different threads (`filum.start`).
## Use `WeakRc`/`WeakArc` to break a cycle: a child points at its parent
## without keeping it alive.
##
## ## When not to use it
## Do not use `Rc` for a value with a single owner: `derive Drop` (layer 1) is
## faster and makes the ownership visible in the type. Do not use `Rc` to
## silence a borrow error that `banish` would model exactly. Do not put a
## `Rc` inside a hot inner loop as a poor man's allocator: the counter is
## shared cache traffic.
##
## ## The cost is in the type
## `Rc` copies implicitly because the copy is one non-atomic increment.
## `Arc` is move-only: a copy is an atomic operation and must be spelled
## `.clone()`. `make_mut` is explicit because it may clone the payload.
##
## ## Example: a shared tree node
## ```pengu
## import std.consortium
## import std.spark
##
## rune Node:
##     value as int
##
## weave main into int:
##     var root as Rc of Node is calling Rc.new with Node { value is 7 }
##     var alias as Rc of Node is root          # one increment
##     calling spark.println with "{(calling alias.get)->value}"
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Implementation
## Every handle is one pointer to the payload. The counter lives in a header
## immediately before it:
## `{ strong, weak, magic, drop, clone, size }`. `pengu_rc_release` runs the
## destructor when `strong` reaches zero and frees the block when `weak` does.
## `tools/build_runtime.sh` recompiles the runtime after changing the header.

## Single-threaded reference-counted handle. Copying is implicit and cheap.
rune Rc shard T derive Drop:
    ## Pointer to the payload; the counter header lives just before it.
    ptr as ref to void

## Non-owning handle for `Rc`. Copying is implicit; it never keeps `T` alive.
rune WeakRc shard T derive Drop:
    ## Pointer to the payload (or to a header whose value is already dead).
    ptr as ref to void

## Multi-threaded reference-counted handle. Move-only: copy with `.clone()`.
rune Arc shard T derive Drop:
    ## Pointer to the payload; the atomic header lives just before it.
    ptr as ref to void

## Non-owning handle for `Arc`.
rune WeakArc shard T derive Drop:
    ## Pointer to the payload (or to a header whose value is already dead).
    ptr as ref to void

antiquus consortium_rc_strong with p as ref to frozen void into int:
    r"""
    return (int)pengu_rc_strong((void *)p);
    """

antiquus consortium_rc_weak with p as ref to frozen void into int:
    r"""
    return (int)pengu_rc_weak_count((void *)p);
    """

antiquus consortium_rc_upgrade with p as ref to frozen void into ref to void:
    r"""
    return pengu_rc_weak_upgrade((void *)p);
    """

antiquus consortium_rc_alive with p as ref to frozen void into bool:
    r"""
    return pengu_rc_weak_alive((void *)p);
    """

antiquus consortium_arc_strong with p as ref to frozen void into int:
    r"""
    return (int)pengu_arc_strong((void *)p);
    """

antiquus consortium_arc_weak with p as ref to frozen void into int:
    r"""
    return (int)pengu_arc_weak_count((void *)p);
    """

antiquus consortium_arc_upgrade with p as ref to frozen void into ref to void:
    r"""
    return pengu_arc_weak_upgrade((void *)p);
    """

antiquus consortium_arc_alive with p as ref to frozen void into bool:
    r"""
    return pengu_arc_weak_alive((void *)p);
    """

antiquus consortium_rc_retain with p as ref to void into ref to void:
    r"""
    return pengu_rc_retain(p);
    """

antiquus consortium_rc_weak_new with p as ref to void into ref to void:
    r"""
    return pengu_rc_weak_new(p);
    """

antiquus consortium_rc_make_mut with p as ref to void into ref to void:
    r"""
    return pengu_rc_make_mut(p);
    """

antiquus consortium_arc_retain with p as ref to void into ref to void:
    r"""
    return pengu_arc_clone(p);
    """

antiquus consortium_arc_weak_new with p as ref to void into ref to void:
    r"""
    return pengu_arc_weak_new(p);
    """

antiquus consortium_arc_make_mut with p as ref to void into ref to void:
    r"""
    return pengu_arc_make_mut(p);
    """

enchanting Rc shard T:
    ## Allocates `value` inside a new reference count (strong = 1).
    ##
    ## The compiler lowers this call to `pengu_rc_new` with the destructor and
    ## the deep copy of `T`, so the body below is only a type-check placeholder.
    weave ritual new with value as T into Rc of T:
        return with ptr is (transmute 0 to ref to void)

    ## The value, without handing out ownership.
    weave get into ref to frozen T:
        return transmute self.ptr to ref to frozen T

    ## The value for writing, only when this is the only owner.
    weave get_mut into maybe ref to T:
        if (calling consortium_rc_strong with self.ptr) == 1 and (calling consortium_rc_weak with self.ptr) == 0:
            return some (transmute self.ptr to ref to T)
        return maybe none

    ## The value for writing, cloning the payload first if it is shared.
    weave make_mut into ref to T:
        set self->ptr is transmute (calling consortium_rc_make_mut with self.ptr) to ref to void
        return transmute self.ptr to ref to T

    ## Number of strong owners (including this one).
    weave strong_count into int:
        return calling consortium_rc_strong with self.ptr

    ## Number of weak observers.
    weave weak_count into int:
        return calling consortium_rc_weak with self.ptr

    ## A non-owning handle to the same value.
    weave downgrade into WeakRc of T:
        return with ptr is transmute (calling consortium_rc_weak_new with self.ptr) to ref to void

    ## One more strong owner.
    weave clone into Rc of T:
        return with ptr is transmute (calling consortium_rc_retain with self.ptr) to ref to void

enchanting Arc shard T:
    ## Allocates `value` inside a new atomic reference count (strong = 1).
    ##
    ## The compiler lowers this call to `pengu_arc_new` with the destructor and
    ## the deep copy of `T`; the body is a type-check placeholder.
    weave ritual new with value as T into Arc of T:
        return with ptr is (transmute 0 to ref to void)

    ## One more strong owner. This is the **only** way to copy an `Arc`.
    weave clone into Arc of T:
        return with ptr is transmute (calling consortium_arc_retain with self.ptr) to ref to void

    ## The value, without handing out ownership.
    weave get into ref to frozen T:
        return transmute self.ptr to ref to frozen T

    ## The value for writing, cloning the payload first if it is shared.
    weave make_mut into ref to T:
        set self->ptr is transmute (calling consortium_arc_make_mut with self.ptr) to ref to void
        return transmute self.ptr to ref to T

    ## Number of strong owners (including this one).
    weave strong_count into int:
        return calling consortium_arc_strong with self.ptr

    ## Number of weak observers.
    weave weak_count into int:
        return calling consortium_arc_weak with self.ptr

    ## A non-owning handle to the same value.
    weave downgrade into WeakArc of T:
        return with ptr is transmute (calling consortium_arc_weak_new with self.ptr) to ref to void

enchanting WeakRc shard T:
    ## The value as a new strong owner, or `none` if it already died.
    weave upgrade into maybe Rc of T:
        var p as ref to void is calling consortium_rc_upgrade with self.ptr
        if (calling consortium_rc_alive with self.ptr):
            var out as Rc of T is with ptr is p
            # El local `out` lleva destructor: la caja se queda con una
            # referencia y el destructor devuelve la que añadimos aquí.
            set out.ptr is (calling consortium_rc_retain with out.ptr)
            return some out
        return maybe none

    ## Whether the value is still alive.
    weave is_alive into bool:
        return calling consortium_rc_alive with self.ptr

    ## Number of strong owners remaining (0 once dead).
    weave strong_count into int:
        return calling consortium_rc_strong with self.ptr

    ## One more weak observer.
    weave clone into WeakRc of T:
        return with ptr is transmute (calling consortium_rc_weak_new with self.ptr) to ref to void

enchanting WeakArc shard T:
    ## The value as a new strong owner, or `none` if it already died.
    weave upgrade into maybe Arc of T:
        var p as ref to void is calling consortium_arc_upgrade with self.ptr
        if (calling consortium_arc_alive with self.ptr):
            var out as Arc of T is with ptr is p
            # El local `out` lleva destructor: la caja se queda con una
            # referencia y el destructor devuelve la que añadimos aquí.
            set out.ptr is (calling consortium_arc_retain with out.ptr)
            return some out
        return maybe none

    ## Whether the value is still alive.
    weave is_alive into bool:
        return calling consortium_arc_alive with self.ptr

    ## Number of strong owners remaining (0 once dead).
    weave strong_count into int:
        return calling consortium_arc_strong with self.ptr

    ## One more weak observer.
    weave clone into WeakArc of T:
        return with ptr is transmute (calling consortium_arc_weak_new with self.ptr) to ref to void
